duced Leukocytosis: Medications (metformin, insulin, buspirone) do not typically cause this magnitude of leukocytosis", "Hyperparathyroidism as Primary Aetiology: Hypercalcemia could indicate this, but systemic symptoms and leukocytosis suggest broader pathology"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Elevated leukocyte count (66,500/mm³)", "Hypercalcemia (10.9 mEq/L)", "Mild fever and hypertension"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.29302458699876277, "posterior": 0.016890736928183703, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal differential with severe leukocytosis moderately supports non-CML myeloproliferative neoplasms like polycythemia vera or essential thrombocythemia."], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAK strongly contradicts CML, which typically presents with low LAK levels."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.102, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of bone pain and Bence-Jones proteinuria weakly contradicts Multiple Myeloma, though the patient’s hemoglobin (12 g/dL) and hematocrit (36%) sugges…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.075, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Chronic presentation and hypercalcemia moderately contradict reacti